                    <h2 class="text-5xl font-bold mt-4">A Guide to Getting a Home Loan if You're Self-Employed</h2>
                </div>
            
                <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto text-slate-600">
                    <p class="lead">Working for yourself has many advantages. But fluctuating earnings can make lenders look closer. The good news — buying a home while self-employed is absolutely possible with the right preparation and team behind you.</p>
                
                    <div class="my-16 bg-emerald-50 rounded-3xl p-10">
                        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6">Start by understanding what you can afford</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-4 text-lg">
                            <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="bg-emerald-200 text-emerald-700 w-6 h-6 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-1">✓</span> Monthly repayment should ideally not exceed 25% of average monthly income</li>
                            <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="bg-emerald-200 text-emerald-700 w-6 h-6 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-1">✓</span> Keep personal and business finances separate</li>
                            <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="bg-emerald-200 text-emerald-700 w-6 h-6 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-1">✓</span> Prepare a deposit to strengthen your application</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                
                    <h3 class="font-semibold text-2xl mb-8">Documents typically required for self-employed applicants:</h3>
                    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                        <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-3xl p-8">
                            <ul class="space-y-5 text-base">
                                <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-lines text-emerald-500"></i> Proof of income + accountant letter</li>
                                <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-lines text-emerald-500"></i> Last 6 months personal &amp; business bank statements</li>
                                <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-lines text-emerald-500"></i> Last 2 years financial statements</li>
                                <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-lines text-emerald-500"></i> Business registration / trust deed (if applicable)</li>
                                <li class="flex gap-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-lines text-emerald-500"></i> Copy of ID</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

